\[
\begin{array}{l}
\text { Acceleration of centre of mass }=\frac{m_{1}(-g)+m_{2}(-g)}{m_{1}+m_{2}} \\
=-g \frac{\left(m_{1}+m_{2}\right)}{\left(m_{1}+m_{2}\right)}=-g
\end{array}
\]<br>Therefore, acceleration of centre of mass of two balls in air is equal to \( \mathrm{g} \), that is, acceleration due to gravity
